---
.title = "Measure and Bound Work with Io Clock and Timeout",
.date = "2026-09-29",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

`std.Io.Clock` provides timestamps from a selected clock. Direct sleeping uses
`std.Io.sleep(io, duration, clock)`; when an operation needs a wait limit, use
`std.Io.Timeout`, which can represent no timeout, a duration, or a deadline,
and call `timeout.sleep(io)`. This example compares direct sleep with timeout
sleep and measures both waits.

